# Kandelo patch rationale (S23)
#
# Native constructors need observations at the real allocation points,
# including nested calls, derived construction and returned replacement
# objects. A single callback at constructor return loses that distinction.
# Keep those generic engine events and scopes. Constructor naming and the
# weak history table now live in the bridge; this patch no longer chooses
# Node-facing names or owns the table.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

